review_comment:
issue: `coordinator.drain()` only runs when `exec()` raises `RerunException` / `StopException`. Any other exception (unhandled user-code error, the defensive `RuntimeError` from `_maybe_handle_execution_control_request`, etc.) bypasses both `join()` and `drain()`, leaving `coordinator._executor` un-shutdown. This is currently harmless because nothing calls `submit()` in this PR, but once dispatch lands in PR 7 it becomes a thread-leak per failing run and may leave worker fragments running after the run is reported as failed. Consider widening to a `try/finally` (or a generic `except BaseException` that drains and re-raises) and adding a regression test covering the generic-exception path:

```python
try:
    if PagesManager.uses_pages_directory:
        _mpa_v1(self._main_script_path)
    else:
        exec(code, module.__dict__)
    coordinator.join()
except BaseException:
    coordinator.drain()
    raise
```

