review_comment:
Race condition bug: If an image is already `complete` but has `naturalWidth === 0` (which occurs when an image fails to load), the code will add event listeners for 'load' and 'error' events that have already fired. This causes the Promise to hang indefinitely, blocking the test.

The condition should check if the image has already errored:

```javascript
if (!img.complete || img.naturalWidth === 0) {
    if (img.complete && img.naturalWidth === 0) {
        throw new Error('Image failed to load');
    }
    await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
        img.addEventListener('load', resolve);
        img.addEventListener('error', reject);
    });
}
```

Alternatively, check the error state before adding listeners to avoid waiting for events that have already occurred.
```suggestion

                    if (!img.complete || img.naturalWidth === 0) {
                        if (img.complete && img.naturalWidth === 0) {
                            throw new Error('Image failed to load');
                        }
                        await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
                            img.addEventListener('load', resolve);
                            img.addEventListener('error', reject);
                        });
                    }

```


