Using `default=None` with `is_flag=True` causes incorrect behavior. In Click, boolean flags should default to False when not provided. With `default=None`, the logic at line 229 checking `if shorthand_val is not None` will incorrectly trigger even when the flag is not provided (since Click sets it to False, not None). Remove the `default=None` parameter from all three flag options.
