`delta_description` is assigned directly into the proto without validation/dedenting. For consistency with `delta`/`help`, validate it’s a `str` (raise a clear error otherwise) and consider `dedent(...)` to avoid unexpected indentation/newlines. Also, if `delta_description` is only meaningful when `delta` is present, consider ignoring/raising when `delta` is empty to avoid silently dropping it in the UI.
```suggestion
            if not isinstance(delta_description, str):
                raise StreamlitAPIException(
                    "`delta_description` must be a string, "
                    f"but got value of type {type(delta_description)}."
                )
            if delta in (None, ""):
                raise StreamlitAPIException(
                    "`delta_description` can only be set when `delta` is provided."
                )
            metric_proto.delta_description = dedent(delta_description)
```

