review_comment:
This mirrors the existing async version's behavior in `_asyncio.py` (lines 234-244), which also catches `anyio.get_cancelled_exc_class()` without re-raising:

```python
finally:
    try:
        await arelease_concurrency_slots_with_lease(lease_id=response.lease_id)
    except anyio.get_cancelled_exc_class():
        if ctx := ConcurrencyContext.get():
            ctx.cleanup_lease_ids.append(response.lease_id)
```

The scenario where the timeout fires during the release (rather than during the task body) is the same in both sync and async — and both versions handle it the same way: defer to `ConcurrencyContext` cleanup. Changing only the sync version to re-raise would introduce an inconsistency.

