review_comment:
You probably need to add every `dvc.lock` file. 
```suggestion
        for file in dvc.scm.untracked_files():
            if os.path.basename(file) == LOCK_FILE:
                include_untracked.append(file)
```

@pared 
>Also, erepo already has few things inside that can be get-ed:
for example:
in case of file: Repo.get(erepo.root_dir, erepo.FOO, "foo_imported")
in case of dir: Repo.get(erepo.root_dir, erepo.DATA_DIR, "dir_imported")

Yes, but those are `dvc add`ed in `erepo` fixture and this PR is aiming to test `get`ing files that are tracked by git and not dvc.

```suggestion
def _copy_git_file(repo, src, dst):
```

diff_hunk:
@@ -268,6 +268,13 @@ def __init__(self, path, cause=None):
         )


+class FileOutsideRepoError(DvcException):

review_comment:
@danihodovic You were saying that 

> I can't get similar logic to fit into this context because of an outer catch clause of OutputNotFoundError.

So I wonder why you can't adjust it to have similar logic so that you don't lookup output twice in your code? I.e. you have find_outs_by_relpath here https://github.com/iterative/dvc/pull/2837/files#diff-d84a7ca40e278c5be8904f9aeb922da0R26 and then here https://github.com/iterative/dvc/pull/2837/files#diff-d84a7ca40e278c5be8904f9aeb922da0R83 . Similar code in Repo.open() has only one find_outs_by_path and is dealing with absolutely the same situation where it has to distinguish cached outs from non-cached outs from git files. So I'm wondering why you can't do something similar here in get()?

Like so?
```py
def _copy_git_file(repo, src, dst, repo_url):
    src_full_path = os.path.join(repo.root_dir, src)
    dst_full_path = os.path.abspath(dst)

    if os.path.isdir(src_full_path):
        shutil.copytree(src_full_path, dst_full_path)
        return

    try:
        shutil.copy2(src_full_path, dst_full_path)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        raise PathOutsideRepoError(src, repo_url)

