review_comment:
`_reify_pact_body()` mutates the passed-in `body` (lists/dicts are modified in place). Since callers pass shared module-level constants (e.g., `GET_DATA_CONTEXT_CONFIGURATION_MIN_RESPONSE_BODY`), this can permanently replace matchers with example values and affect later tests/interaction definitions. Consider returning a new structure (e.g., build new dict/list or `copy.deepcopy()` first) instead of mutating the input.
```suggestion
    if isinstance(body, match.AbstractMatcher):
        return _reify_pact_body(body=_convert_matcher_to_value(matcher=body))
    elif isinstance(body, list):
        return [_reify_pact_body(body=item) for item in body]
    elif isinstance(body, dict):
        return {key: _reify_pact_body(body=value) for key, value in body.items()}
```

