@timgraham you (and Claude) are right that ordering by outer field has no impact as it's _constant_ from the subquery perspective (the `Book` subquery is run once per `Publisher` and `num_awards` is constant per publisher). This means that the ordering is effectively undefined in this case as well.

The test do capture the crash though which was caused by `Aggregate.resolve_expression` double resolving of `order_by` expressions. The thing is only `OuterRef` is sensitive to this kind of problem as once field referenced are resolved to `Col` instances extra resolving will always be noops.

To summarize, yes the ordering in nonsensical (as it's against a constant value) from a semantic perspective but it's the only way to reproduce the reported crash.

