review_comment:
@felixxm If we hard code the signature(or any other attribute), then this test case need to be updated every time the original function's signature, docstring, etc are updated. To avoid that can I do the below? Moreover, our goal is to ensure manager methods show the same signature and docstrings as the queryset methods and not a specific string.
```python3
    def test_manager_methods_attributes(self):
        for method in self.QUERYSET_PROXY_METHODS:
            manager_method = getattr(Article.objects, method)
            queryset_method = getattr(models.QuerySet, method)

            self.assertEqual(
                str(inspect.signature(manager_method)),
                str(inspect.signature(queryset_method)).replace('self, ', '').replace('self', '')
            )
            
            self.assertEqual(
                manager_method.__doc__,
                queryset_method.__doc__
            )

            self.assertEqual(
                manager_method.__annotations__,
                queryset_method.__annotations__
            )
```

